commit 64bb25a78b2e9e0866ca4da4d07e4658860ed4d3
Author: ledger <ledger@example.invalid>
Date:   Mon Nov 23 01:38:38 2026 +0000

    Add tasks and polytunnel watering boards
    
    Both read incoming/tasks.csv directly so the sheet stays the one copy
    (the polytunnel swap in September went wrong because of a second copy).
    Tasks: one box per person, soonest first, overdue marked, unowned jobs
    in their own box, done jobs folded. Rota: one box per week, current
    week badged, past weeks folded.
    
    kit/board.py gains opt-in settings for this; the events board builds
    byte-identically to before (checked on three dates).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index a51b234..67a3195 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -8,6 +8,19 @@ board shows), a CSV data file, and the built page `index.html`.
 
 - `boards/events/`: the society's events (AGM, open day, plant sale) and what each one
   still needs.
+- `boards/tasks/`: the committee's task sheet, one box per person with their jobs
+  soonest first, a box for jobs with nobody's name on them, and done jobs folded away.
+- `boards/polytunnel-watering/`: whose week it is to water the polytunnel.
+
+The tasks and polytunnel boards both read the sheet's export, `incoming/tasks.csv`,
+directly (the rota is the two columns at the side). When a new export lands there,
+rebuild both:
+
+    python3 kit/board.py boards/tasks
+    python3 kit/board.py boards/polytunnel-watering
+
+"Overdue" on the tasks board is worked out when the page is built, so rebuild before
+each Thursday meeting even if the sheet hasn't changed.
 
